/home/drx/.cache/mipstarre-dev/sessions/orc-748-20261002-01.jsonl:39:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n \\\"Exact ownership inventory|EvaluatedQuestions\\\\.lean|packet748|P3\\\" local results /home/drx/.cache/mipstarre-dev/sessions 2>/dev/null | head -n 120\"","aggregated_output":"results/telemetry/palomar-pilot-ci-20261002.md:59:now also depends on #756. P3 and P4 can proceed concurrently after P2.\n/home/drx/.cache/mipstarre-dev/sessions/scout-733-20260929-01.jsonl:47:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_24\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat /home/drx/.cache/mipstarre-dev/sessions/scout-727-20260929-02.last.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"Recommend **two additive LDT improvements**:\\n\\n1. Replace the two final-theorem consistency triangles by a linear-error triangle. A concrete, mathematically derived target is\\n   \\\\[\\n   \\\\boxed{\\\\min\\\\!\\\\left\\\\{1,\\\\;\\n   10000\\\\,k^{1/4}m^{1/2}\\n   \\\\left(\\\\varepsilon^{1/8192}+(d/q)^{1/8192}\\n   +e^{-k/(640000m^2)}\\\\right)\\\\right\\\\}.}\\n   \\\\]\\n2. Replace the additive Hoeffding estimate in pasting by a multiplicative Bernoulli estimate, improving its tail from\\n   \\\\[\\n   e^{-k/(80000m^2)}\\\\quad\\\\text{to}\\\\quad e^{-k/(1600m)}.\\n   \\\\]\\n\\nThese are **unformalized improvements with concrete proof plans**, not newly proved Lean results. The first changes the headline exponent and polynomial scaling without rebuilding the induction. The second improves the induction’s exponential dependence on dimension.\\n\\nSurveyed snapshot: `7bdfa416b7ff1f4a19de98b915efb3ca940f6fd9`. This session changed nothing and used no subagents.\\n\\n**The exact existing baseline.**\\n\\nWrite \\\\(r=d/q\\\\). The current public declarations are:\\n\\n| Declaration | Existing bound | Public domain and conclusion |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| [`MainInductionStep.mainInduction`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/MainInductionStep/Theorems/MainTheorems/Successor.lean:308) | \\\\(I=m^2\\\\left(1000k^2m^2(\\\\varepsilon^{1/1024}+\\\\delta^{1/1024}+\\\\gamma^{1/1024}+r^{1/1024})+e^{-k/(80000m^2)}\\\\right)\\\\) | Good symmetric strategy; \\\\(k\\\\ge400md\\\\). Produces a complete polynomial measurement consistent with points. |\\n| [`Test.mainFormal`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/Test/MainTheorem/MainFormal.lean:300) | \\\\(B=100000k^2m^4(\\\\varepsilon^{1/40000}+r^{1/40000}+e^{-k/(2560000m^2)})\\\\) | General two-space projective strategy passing with failure at most \\\\(\\\\varepsilon\\\\); \\\\(k\\\\ge400md\\\\), \\\\(k>0\\\\). Produces two projective polynomial measurements and all three final consistency conclusions. |\\n\\nThe error definitions are [`mainInductionNu` / `mainInductionError`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/MainInductionStep/Defs.lean:467) and [`mainFormalError`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/Test/MainTheorem/ScalarBounds/Definitions.lean:32).\\n\\nParameters have \\\\(m\\\\ge1\\\\), prime-power \\\\(q\\\\ge2\\\\), and \\\\(d\\\\in\\\\mathbb N\\\\), including zero. Normalization and line-reparametrization covariance are bundled in the strategy. No public \\\\(d\\\\le q\\\\), \\\\(k\\\\le q\\\\), or unit-interval error restriction is assumed.\\n\\nThe corresponding paper statements are `thm:main-formal` in `test_definition.tex:180–202` and `thm:main-induction` in `inductive_step.tex:7–17`. Both print \\\\(k\\\\ge md\\\\). **The current Lean baseline has a documented stronger sampling hypothesis**, not that printed domain. See [issue-906’s correction](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/docs/paper-gaps/issue-906-main-formal-k-bound.tex:160) and [the zero-sampling correction](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/docs/paper-gaps/issue-422-main-formal-zero-k-boundary.tex).\\n\\nBefore implementing an improvement, add explicit baseline corollaries by unfolding these error definitions. There are no existential constants to resolve in the LDT headlines themselves. Add the corollaries to the axiom audits without changing existing declarations.\\n\\n**What the current proof actually carries.**\\n\\nThe final construction has a more informative bound than its public envelope. Put\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\nI&=\\\\operatorname{mainInductionError}(m,q,d,k;3\\\\varepsilon,3\\\\varepsilon,3\\\\varepsilon),\\\\\\\\\\ns&=2I,\\\\\\\\\\nz&=s+2\\\\sqrt{3\\\\varepsilon+s}+mr,\\\\\\\\\\no&=100z^{1/4},\\\\\\\\\\nc&=2o+4\\\\sqrt o+2z\\n   =200z^{1/4}+40z^{1/8}+2z,\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\eta&=z+\\\\sqrt o=z+10z^{1/8},\\\\\\\\\\nv&=6z+6c.\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n\\\\]\\n[`sourceRoleRegisterFinalPointConsistency`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/Test/MainTheorem/SourceRoleRegister/Final.lean:334) constructs the **same witnesses** with point-consistency errors\\n\\\\[\\ns+2\\\\sqrt{\\\\eta+v/2}\\n\\\\]\\nand full-polynomial consistency error \\\\(v/2\\\\).\\n\\nTwo repairs must remain in any new calculation:\\n\\n- Completion contributes \\\\(+2z\\\\). The existing scalar cascade absorbs it by using \\\\(200z^{1/4}+42z^{1/8}\\\\).\\n- The repaired line-169 transfer uses \\\\(\\\\eta=z+10z^{1/8}\\\\), not the paper’s printed \\\\(z\\\\).\\n\\nThe current scalar proof obtains the intermediate coefficients\\n\\\\[\\n20204,\\\\quad2568,\\\\quad150000,\\n\\\\]\\nfor its successive \\\\(z_1,z_2,z_3\\\\) envelopes. The repaired final point estimate passes through\\n\\\\[\\n(20000+826)k^2m^4E_{32768}\\n\\\\le40000k^2m^4E_{32768}.\\n\\\\]\\nFull-polynomial consistency is bounded by \\\\(75000k^2m^4E_{16384}\\\\). Only afterward are both weakened to the public coefficient \\\\(100000\\\\) and exponent \\\\(1/40000\\\\). See [the repaired final calculation](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/Test/MainTheorem/ScalarBounds/CascadeBounds/Zeta4.lean:199).\\n\\nThus the existing exponent losses are\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\frac1{1024}\\n\\\\longrightarrow\\\\frac1{2048}\\n\\\\longrightarrow\\\\frac1{8192}\\n\\\\longrightarrow\\\\frac1{16384}\\n\\\\longrightarrow\\\\frac1{32768}\\n\\\\longrightarrow\\\\frac1{40000}.\\n\\\\]\\nThe first and penultimate arrows arise from the two consistency triangles targeted below.\\n\\n**Dependency-ordered coverage.**\\n\\nThis was an audit of numerical interfaces and their relevant proof paths, not a line-by-line review of every private lemma.\\n\\n| Submodule | Verified quantitative content and qualifications |\\n|---|---|\\n| Setup and preliminaries | Three equally weighted subtests give \\\\((3\\\\varepsilon,3\\\\varepsilon,3\\\\varepsilon)\\\\); unsymmetrization costs a factor two. `SDDRel` bounds **squared** state-dependent distance. [`simeqToApprox_heterogeneous`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/Preliminaries/ComparisonCore.lean:201) costs \\\\(2\\\\delta\\\\); the projective converse divides by two. Paper: `prop:simeq-to-approx`, `prop:simeq-triangle-inequality`. |\\n| Projectivization | The measurement lemma already proves \\\\(84\\\\zeta^{1/4}\\\\); the final route uses \\\\(100\\\\zeta^{1/4}\\\\). The separate \\\\(120\\\\zeta^{1/4}\\\\) completion-route theorem is **not** the headline’s chosen bound. See [`orthonormalizationMainLemma`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/MakingMeasurementsProjective/Orthonormalization.lean:27). Paper: `lem:orthonormalization-main-lemma`, `thm:orthonormalization`. |\\n| Expansion | [`localToGlobal`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/ExpansionHypercubeGraph/Theorems/Results.lean:311) has factor \\\\(m\\\\), matching the spectral gap. This factor is sharp for families depending on one coordinate. Paper: `lem:local-to-global`. |\\n| Global variance | Local six-step transport gives \\\\(6(4\\\\varepsilon+4\\\\delta+2mr)\\\\), weakened to \\\\(24(\\\\varepsilon+\\\\delta+mr)\\\\); global variance multiplies by \\\\(m\\\\). Polynomial outcomes are summed without a polynomial-cardinality loss. See [error definitions](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/GlobalVariance/Defs/Families.lean:352). Paper: `lem:generalize-b`, `lem:local-variance-of-points`, `lem:global-variance-of-points`. |\\n| Self-improvement | Set \\\\(h=100m(\\\\sqrt\\\\varepsilon+\\\\sqrt\\\\delta+\\\\sqrt r)\\\\), \\\\(o=100h^{1/4}\\\\), \\\\(t=8h+8\\\\sqrt o\\\\). The checked completeness, point, self-distance and boundedness budgets include respectively \\\\(2h+2\\\\sqrt o\\\\), \\\\(2h+\\\\sqrt t+2\\\\sqrt o\\\\), \\\\(6h+6o\\\\), and \\\\(h+\\\\sqrt t\\\\). They are absorbed into \\\\(3000m(\\\\varepsilon^{1/32}+\\\\delta^{1/32}+r^{1/32})\\\\). See [definitions](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/SelfImprovement/Defs.lean:340) and [thresholds](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/SelfImprovement/Theorems/Thresholds/Final.lean:471). Input \\\\(G\\\\) is a **complete measurement**, matching the proved Section 9 version; the induction-section restatement prints a submeasurement. |\\n| Point commutativity | \\\\(32m\\\\gamma\\\\), from four distance comparisons of size \\\\(2m\\\\gamma\\\\). See [`commutativityPoints`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/CommutativityPoints/BridgeTheorems/DropBridges.lean:290). Paper: `thm:commutativity-points`. |\\n| Polynomial commutativity | Evaluated bound \\\\(48m(\\\\sqrt\\\\gamma+\\\\sqrt\\\\zeta)\\\\). The actual earlier calculation is \\\\(24\\\\sqrt\\\\zeta+24\\\\sqrt{\\\\gamma(m+1)}\\\\). Full-polynomial transport uses \\\\(16\\\\sqrt\\\\zeta+4mr+2\\\\sqrt{\\\\nu_{\\\\rm eval}}\\\\), then \\\\(30m(\\\\gamma^{1/4}+\\\\zeta^{1/4}+r^{1/4})\\\\). The raw coefficients differ from the paper’s displayed arithmetic. See [evaluated chain](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/Commutativity/ScalarApproximation/ProcessedG/MainChain.lean:162) and [full transport](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/Commutativity/Main/EvaluatedQuestions.lean:94). |\\n| Pasting | Complete-part commutation: \\\\(36m\\\\) times a \\\\(1/16\\\\)-power sum; completed-family commutation: \\\\(138m\\\\); commuting through \\\\(k\\\\) slices: \\\\(426k^2m\\\\). Subsequent coefficients are \\\\(43km\\\\), \\\\(44k^2m\\\\), and \\\\(46k^2m\\\\), with exponent \\\\(1/32\\\\). The corrected `fromHToGError` is also **quadratic** in \\\\(k\\\\). Two \\\\(46\\\\)-budgets are absorbed into \\\\(100k^2m\\\\). See [all error definitions](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/Pasting/Statements.lean:34). |\\n| Induction | Self-improvement contributes exponent \\\\(1/32\\\\), followed by pasting’s \\\\(1/32\\\\), producing \\\\(1/1024\\\\). Slice restriction costs \\\\((m+1)/m\\\\), handled by concavity. The actual scalar proof establishes \\\\(\\\\nu_{\\\\rm paste}\\\\le\\\\nu_{\\\\rm induction}/5\\\\), stronger than merely \\\\(\\\\le\\\\nu_{\\\\rm induction}\\\\). See [`ldPastingInInductionNu_le_fifth_mainInductionNu`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/MainInductionStep/Theorems/PastingAssembly/Basic.lean:31). The headline runs through answer-valued strong induction. |\\n\\n**Candidate inventory.**\\n\\nAll proposed gains below are unimplemented. “Extraction” means the sharper estimate is already visible inside an existing proof; it still needs an additive public theorem and downstream wiring.\\n\\n| Candidate and exact location | Current → proposed; domain | Mechanism, effect, cost/risk |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **1. Linear consistency triangle.** [`simeqTriangleInequality_heterogeneous`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/Preliminaries/Triangles/SimEq.lean:125); paper/blueprint `prop:simeq-triangle-inequality` | \\\\(\\\\alpha+2\\\\sqrt{\\\\beta+\\\\gamma}\\\\) → \\\\(3(\\\\alpha+\\\\beta+\\\\gamma)\\\\), for complete measurements. | New elementary defect identity plus the existing three-step distance triangle. Removes two headline square roots; detailed bound below. Medium implementation cost; low mathematical risk after independent review. |\\n| **2. Multiplicative Bernoulli tail.** [`bernoulliTailLowerAffine_le_scalarBernoulliTail`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/Pasting/Bernoulli/Scalar.lean:438); paper/blueprint `lem:chernoff-bernoulli-matrix` | \\\\(e^{-\\\\theta^2k/2}\\\\) → \\\\(e^{-\\\\theta k/8}\\\\), retaining \\\\(0<\\\\theta<1\\\\), \\\\(k\\\\ge2d/\\\\theta\\\\). At \\\\(\\\\theta=1/(200m)\\\\): denominator \\\\(80000m^2\\\\to1600m\\\\). | Binomial exponential moment, then existing CFC construction. Improves induction and final exponential scaling. Medium/high wiring cost; low scalar mathematical risk. |\\n| **3. Preserve roots of polynomial prefactors.** [`sourceRoleRegisterFinalPointConsistency`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/Test/MainTheorem/SourceRoleRegister/Final.lean:334); paper `inductive_step.tex:186–234` | Existing headline → \\\\(\\\\min(1,200k^{1/16}m^{1/8}E_{32768})\\\\), with the old exponential denominator \\\\(2560000m^2\\\\). Same headline domain. | Calculational consequence of the existing construction and the defect bound \\\\(1\\\\). Low/medium cost. A useful fallback, but candidate 1 is stronger in exponent. |\\n| **4. Linear accumulation over dimensions.** [`ldPastingInInductionError_le_mainInductionError_of_bounds`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/MainInductionStep/Theorems/PastingAssembly/ErrorBounds.lean:25); paper `thm:main-induction` | \\\\(m^2(\\\\nu+E_m)\\\\to(2m-1)(\\\\nu+E_m)\\\\). Same induction domain. | Existing \\\\(\\\\nu_{\\\\rm paste}\\\\le\\\\nu/5\\\\) makes a linear recurrence sufficient. Strict improvement for \\\\(m>1\\\\); leading polynomial dependence becomes \\\\(O(k^2m^3)\\\\). Medium/high cost because the answer-valued induction must carry the new bound. |\\n| **5. Remove axis-line degree padding.** [`axisLinePolynomialAgreement_avg_le_mdq`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/Preliminaries/PolynomialAgreement.lean:225); paper `lem:generalize-b` | \\\\(md/q\\\\to d/q\\\\) for distinct axis-line polynomials; then \\\\(24m(\\\\varepsilon+\\\\delta+md/q)\\\\to24m(\\\\varepsilon+\\\\delta+d/q)\\\\). | The proof already obtains \\\\(d/q\\\\) before deliberately padding by \\\\(m\\\\). Extraction uses `Polynomial.card_le_degree_of_subset_roots`. Low local cost; medium propagation cost. Genuine LDT variance gain even without QPBT propagation. |\\n| **6. Retain sharper projectivization/completion constants.** [`orthonormalizationMainLemma`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/MakingMeasurementsProjective/Orthonormalization.lean:27), [`completedCloseness_left_of_consistency_and_sdd`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/Test/MainTheorem/SourceRoleRegister/Completion.lean:395); paper `lem:orthonormalization-main-lemma`, `inductive_step.tex:143–149` | \\\\(100z^{1/4}\\\\to84z^{1/4}\\\\); independently the actual heterogeneous completion proof gives \\\\(2o+2\\\\sqrt o+2z\\\\), before weakening to \\\\(2o+4\\\\sqrt o+2z\\\\). | Existing-proof extraction. Low/medium cost; coefficient gains, no exponent gain. Candidate 1 below conservatively uses the old constants. |\\n| **7. Retain evaluated commutator scaling.** [`evaluatedSlice_scalar_chain_bound`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/Commutativity/ScalarApproximation/ProcessedG/MainChain.lean:162); paper `lem:comm-data-processed-g` | \\\\(48m(\\\\sqrt\\\\gamma+\\\\sqrt\\\\zeta)\\\\to24\\\\sqrt\\\\zeta+24\\\\sqrt{\\\\gamma(m+1)}\\\\). | Extraction before the final weakening. Improves the dimension dependence of this intermediate estimate. Low local cost, larger propagation cost; no automatic change to fixed downstream envelopes. |\\n| **8. Exact distinct-sampling loss.** [`ldDnoteq`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/Pasting/Core/DDistinct.lean:17); paper `prop:ld-dnoteq` | For \\\\(k\\\\le q\\\\), \\\\(k^2/q\\\\to1-(q)_k/q^k\\\\le\\\\min(1,k(k-1)/(2q))\\\\). | Exact identity and pair-count bound already occur in the proof. Low cost, mostly coefficient improvement. Must preserve the separate empty-support case \\\\(k>q\\\\). |\\n\\nTwo tempting changes are not supported:\\n\\n- The expansion factor \\\\(m\\\\) is sharp.\\n- Restoring the paper’s linear-in-\\\\(k\\\\) `fromHToGError` is not a valid optimization: the actual telescope includes \\\\(k\\\\sqrt{\\\\nu_4(k)}\\\\), and \\\\(\\\\nu_4(k)\\\\) already contains \\\\(k^2\\\\).\\n\\nEliminating the induction exponent \\\\(1/1024\\\\) would require new self-improvement or pasting analysis. I found no comparably bounded proof plan for that.\\n\\n**Rank 1: a linear consistency triangle and its explicit headline.**\\n\\nFor complete measurements on the common bipartite space, write\\n\\\\[\\nu_A=\\\\mathbb E_x\\\\sum_a\\\\langle A_a^x-(A_a^x)^2\\\\rangle\\\\ge0,\\n\\\\]\\nand let \\\\(D_{AB}\\\\) denote squared state-dependent distance between the placed families. Completeness gives the exact identity\\n\\\\[\\n2C_{AB}=D_{AB}+u_A+u_B.\\n\\\\]\\n\\nApply the existing three-step distance triangle:\\n\\\\[\\nD_{AD}\\\\le3(D_{AB}+D_{BC}+D_{CD}).\\n\\\\]\\nSubstitution yields\\n\\\\[\\n2C_{AD}\\n\\\\le6(C_{AB}+C_{BC}+C_{CD})\\n -2u_A-6u_B-6u_C-2u_D,\\n\\\\]\\nhence\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{C_{AD}\\\\le3(C_{AB}+C_{BC}+C_{CD}).}\\n\\\\]\\n\\nThis avoids assuming that approximate distance alone implies consistency for nonprojective measurements. The nonnegative projectivity defects supply the missing terms. It also does **not** reinstate the coefficient-one inequality that the paper identifies as incorrect.\\n\\nAvailable support:\\n\\n- [`qBipartiteConsDefect_of_measurements`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/Test/StrategyRole/Algebra.lean:96).\\n- [`questionSDD_triangle_three`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/Preliminaries/DistanceBounds.lean:46).\\n- Existing squared-effect bounds and expansion algebra in [`ComparisonCore.lean`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/Preliminaries/ComparisonCore.lean:63).\\n- `Quantum.sq_le_self`, positivity of expectations, and averaging linearity.\\n\\nCompleteness is essential. Extending this lemma to arbitrary submeasurements would be false: zero intermediate submeasurements can make all three input consistency defects vanish.\\n\\nFor the headline, retain \\\\(s=2I\\\\), but replace the first triangle’s error by\\n\\\\[\\nz=6s+9\\\\varepsilon+mr.\\n\\\\]\\nReuse the existing projectivization, completion, repaired line-169 transfer and evaluation machinery, with\\n\\\\[\\nc=200z^{1/4}+40z^{1/8}+2z,\\\\qquad\\n\\\\eta=z+10z^{1/8},\\\\qquad v=6z+6c.\\n\\\\]\\nApply the new triangle again at the final point step. Its error becomes\\n\\\\[\\nP=3(s+\\\\eta+v/2)\\n =3s+30z+1800z^{1/4}+390z^{1/8}.\\n\\\\]\\nFull-polynomial consistency remains bounded by\\n\\\\[\\nQ=v/2=9z+600z^{1/4}+120z^{1/8}.\\n\\\\]\\n\\nFor \\\\(0\\\\le z\\\\le1\\\\), \\\\(s\\\\le z/6\\\\), so\\n\\\\[\\nP,Q\\\\le2221z^{1/8}.\\n\\\\]\\nFor \\\\(z>1\\\\), the universal consistency bound \\\\(1\\\\) supplies the complementary branch.\\n\\nNow set\\n\\\\[\\nE=\\\\varepsilon^{1/1024}+r^{1/1024}+e^{-k/(80000m^2)}.\\n\\\\]\\nOn \\\\(0\\\\le\\\\varepsilon,r\\\\le1\\\\), the existing [`mainFormalInductionNu_bound`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/Test/MainTheorem/SourceScalars.lean:98) gives\\n\\\\[\\nI\\\\le10000k^2m^4E,\\\\qquad z\\\\le120010k^2m^4E.\\n\\\\]\\nThe exact numerical certificates are\\n\\\\[\\n120010\\\\le(9/2)^8,\\\\qquad2221(9/2)=9994.5\\\\le10000.\\n\\\\]\\nSubadditivity of the eighth root therefore proves the proposed headline\\n\\\\[\\nP,Q\\\\le\\n10000k^{1/4}m^{1/2}\\n\\\\left(\\\\varepsilon^{1/8192}+r^{1/8192}\\n+e^{-k/(640000m^2)}\\\\right),\\n\\\\]\\nwith truncation at one. If \\\\(\\\\varepsilon>1\\\\) or \\\\(r>1\\\\), this proposed untruncated bound already exceeds one.\\n\\nRelative to the current baseline, this gives:\\n\\n| Quantity | Current | Proposed |\\n|---|---:|---:|\\n| Coefficient | \\\\(100000\\\\) | \\\\(10000\\\\) |\\n| Power of \\\\(k\\\\) | \\\\(2\\\\) | \\\\(1/4\\\\) |\\n| Power of \\\\(m\\\\) outside the tail | \\\\(4\\\\) | \\\\(1/2\\\\) |\\n| Error/field exponent | \\\\(1/40000\\\\) | \\\\(1/8192\\\\) |\\n| Tail denominator | \\\\(2560000m^2\\\\) | \\\\(640000m^2\\\\) |\\n\\nThe clipped proposed bound is no larger than the clipped baseline throughout the existing headline domain.\\n\\nSuggested additive API:\\n\\n1. `Preliminaries.consistency_triangle_three_heterogeneous`.\\n2. A new full-polynomial consistency theorem beside `sourceRoleRegisterFullPolynomialSelfConsistency_ofPointConsistency`, returning \\\\(6s+9\\\\varepsilon+mr\\\\).\\n3. A new final construction assembled from the existing generic completion and line-169 lemmas.\\n4. `Test.mainFormalLinearTriangleError` and `Test.main_formal_linear_triangle_bound`.\\n5. Explicit baseline and new headline audit entries.\\n\\nDo not reuse `mainFormal_smallErrorConclusion` as the construction for the new theorem: it has already absorbed the estimates into the old error. Start from the unsymmetrized witnesses and generic construction lemmas.\\n\\nEstimated cost: one moderate implementation tranche plus mathematical review. The main risk is formalizing the defect identity and preserving the same witnesses across all three conclusions; the matrix construction itself is already available.\\n\\n**Rank 2: multiplicative Bernoulli decay.**\\n\\nThe current scalar result is [`scalarBernoulliTail_hoeffding_lower_bound`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/Pasting/Bernoulli/Scalar.lean:394), followed by the affine lower bound and [`chernoffBernoulliMatrix`](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/MIPStarRE/LDT/Pasting/Bernoulli/MatrixChernoff.lean:79). The source is `ld-pasting.tex:1671–1795`, `lem:chernoff-bernoulli-matrix`.\\n\\nFor \\\\(Y\\\\sim\\\\mathrm{Binomial}(k,p)\\\\) and \\\\(d\\\\le kp/2\\\\),\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\n\\\\Pr(Y\\\\le d)\\n&\\\\le e^d\\\\,\\\\mathbb E[e^{-Y}]\\\\\\\\\\n&=e^d(1-p+p/e)^k\\\\\\\\\\n&\\\\le e^{d-5kp/8}\\\\\\\\\\n&\\\\le e^{-kp/8}.\\n\\\\end{aligned}\\n\\\\]\\nHere \\\\(e^{-1}\\\\le3/8\\\\) follows from\\n\\\\(e\\\\ge1+1+1/2+1/6=8/3\\\\).\\n\\nUnder the existing size condition \\\\(k\\\\ge2d/\\\\theta\\\\), every \\\\(p\\\\ge\\\\theta\\\\) satisfies \\\\(d\\\\le kp/2\\\\). Therefore\\n\\\\[\\nF_{k,d}(p)\\\\ge\\n1-\\\\frac{1-p}{1-\\\\theta}-e^{-\\\\theta